course: dictionary
lesson: 5006
title: Infect: one word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words change their meaning depending on what you are reading about. Infect is one of them. Read the words around it to find out which meaning fits. «Washing your hands stops germs from infecting you» is about health, so infect means getting germs into your body so that you become ill.
explain: Infect is a verb, so its forms change: infect, infects, infected, infecting. «A cut that becomes red, hot, swollen or full of pus may be infected.» The clues are cut, red, swollen and pus, so infected means the cut has germs in it and has gone bad.
explain: Infect can also be about feelings and computers. «Her laughter infected everyone» means the laughter spread to everyone, so they all started laughing too. «Viruses can infect computers» is about a virus getting into a computer. Always check: put your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
fact: Infect means to get germs into a person, an animal, a cut, or a computer.
fact: Infect can also mean to spread a feeling to other people, like laughter or excitement.
fact: Germs such as bacteria and viruses can infect people, so washing your hands helps stop them spreading.
fact: «Infected» is the past form of infect, as in «The cut became infected».
fact: A cut that becomes red, hot, swollen or full of pus may be infected, so tell a parent or carer.
exercise: «Washing your hands stops germs from infecting you.» What does infect mean here? | To tell a joke | To wash something until it is clean | *To get germs into your body and make you ill | To make something shiny
exercise: «Her laughter infected everyone in the room.» What does infected mean here? | Made them all sick | Locked them in the room | *Spread to everyone, so they all started laughing | Made the room colder
exercise: «Clean a cut so it does not get infected.» What could happen to the cut if it is not cleaned? | It grows longer | It turns into a bird | It becomes too dry to heal | *Germs get in and make it sore
test: «Viruses can infect computers.» What does infect mean in this sentence? | *A virus gets into a computer and causes problems | To make the computer bigger | To switch the computer off | To clean the computer screen
test: «Yesterday the cut ___ because it was dirty.» Which form of infect fits the gap? | infecting | infect | infects | *infected
exam: Which sentence uses infect to mean spread a feeling? | «The bus was late this morning.» | *«Her laughter infected everyone in the room.» | «The computer was switched on.» | «The cut needed a plaster.»
